final_answer:
Molina Healthcare offers a comprehensive suite of benefits to eligible employees, which likely impacts retention and competitiveness. These benefits include:

- Comprehensive health insurance coverage for employees working 30 hours or more per week, with no increase in employee contributions for 2023 and 2024;
- 401(k) employer matching contributions of up to 100% on the first 4% contributed by the employee;
- Personal time off combining vacation and sick leave;
- Volunteer time off for community engagement;
- Employee wellness programs focusing on physical, emotional, financial, and work well-being;
- Up to ten dependent-care back-up visits per year for a low co-pay and homework/tutoring support for children;
- Employee discount programs, including tuition reimbursement;
- Employee assistance program benefits that provide up to six confidential counseling sessions per year, covering physical, emotional, and financial matters.

These HR initiatives support employee well-being, work-life balance, and professional development, which are essential factors in retaining talent and maintaining a competitive edge. By investing in such programs, Molina Healthcare enhances its ability to attract and retain employees, thereby supporting overall company performance.
